module bankr-ri-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frbp9006.{ frbp9006 }
import frbp.events.{ FirstMeetingDate, OrderForReliefEntered, PetitionFiled }

// The Bankr. D.R.I. court's own periods, counted under FRBP 9006(a). The
// FRBP periods (schedules and statements within 14 days, R.I. LBR
// 1007-1(c); the involuntary creditor list within 7 days of the order for
// relief, R.I. LBR 1002-1(c)(4); the 28 days' notice of a chapter 9 or 11
// confirmation hearing, R.I. LBR 3020-1(a)(3); the 14 days before a final
// cash collateral hearing, R.I. LBR 4001-2(d)(3); claims, discharge,
// dischargeability, the adversary answer and summons, appeals) are
// lit/frbp's and are not declared again, nor is the subchapter V report 14
// days before the status conference, which is 11 U.S.C. § 1188(c)'s (R.I.
// LBR 3016-1(a)(1) as amended December 1, 2025). R.I. LBR 1019-1(b) gives
// a chapter 13 trustee 60 days after conversion for the final report and
// account where FRBP 1019(e)(2)(B) gives 30 days unless the court orders
// otherwise; the national period is lit/frbp's to declare, and the local
// one is not declared here.
//
// Layers, in date order, over the Local Bankruptcy Rules as amended
// December 1, 2024: General Order 2025-001 amends R.I. LBR 9010-1 from June
// 3, 2025; General Order 2025-002 amends R.I. LBR 1006-1, 5005-4 and 5079-1
// from July 21, 2025 (clean text vendored; no period changes); General
// Order 2025-003 amends R.I. LBR 1005-1, 3002-1 and 3016-1 from December 1,
// 2025 (clean text vendored; it adds the 28-day response time of R.I. LBR
// 1005-1(d)(2)(Q)); General Order 2026-001 amends R.I. LBR 1005-1, 5005-4,
// "5701-1" (no such rule; R.I. LBR 5071-1, continuances, is the likely
// target, whose clock-time periods are not declared) and Appendix III from
// February 13, 2026. The court posted no text for General Orders 2025-001
// and 2026-001 (sources/bankr-ri/PROVENANCE.md), so each period of a rule
// they amend has a version from the order's date whose cite is a hole: the
// value is the last vendored text's, unverified.
//
// Stated in the rules but not declared: the later installments of a filing
// fee every 28 days (R.I. LBR 1006-1(d)); the clerk's own notices (R.I. LBR
// 2002-1(d)); business-day, hour and clock-time periods (one business day
// for a rent deposit, R.I. LBR 4001-4(a); 48 hours before a chapter 13
// confirmation hearing, R.I. LBR 3015-3(a); 24 hours to serve a chapter 13
// plan, R.I. LBR 3015-1(b); three business days for a stay-relief pretrial
// statement, R.I. LBR 4001-1(g), (i); 3:00 p.m. the day before a hearing,
// R.I. LBR 5005-4(o), 5071-1; four business days for a contested continuance,
// R.I. LBR 5071-1, 1005-1(d)(2)(K); two business days for amendments to a
// matter set for hearing, R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)(4); four business days for a
// draft joint pretrial statement, R.I. LBR 9014-1(c)(1); certificates of
// service the next business day, R.I. LBR 9013-3(e)(2)); the retainer
// draw-down waiting period of 14 days after an itemized bill (R.I. LBR
// 2016-1(i)(1)); the clerk's scheduling of hearings no less than 14 days
// out (R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)(3)); and the 35 days' notice of a continued
// confirmation hearing after an adverse amended plan (R.I. LBR
// 3015-2(b)(1)(B)(iii)). Three objection periods run on the later of two
// dates (R.I. LBR 1009-1(c)(1)(C), 2014-1(c), 2015-3(a), 3007-1(a)); each
// is declared from the event the rule names, and where it names two, from
// each, the later controlling. A paper served by mail gets 3 more days
// under FRBP 9006(f), as the rules' notice language says.
/// An initial motion, response, brief or memorandum of law (R.I. LBR
/// 9013-1(b)).
limit motion-paper { pages <= 20 cite "R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)" } cite "R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)"
/// A reply brief (R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)).
limit reply-brief { pages <= 10 cite "R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)" } cite "R.I. LBR 9013-1(b)"

/// An order denying an application to waive the chapter 7 filing fee is
/// entered (R.I. LBR 1006-1(g)).
event FeeWaiverDenied()
/// A chapter 7 case whose filing fee was waived is converted to another
/// chapter (R.I. LBR 1006-1(h)).
event ConvertedFromWaivedChapter7()
/// The schedules of liabilities are filed in a chapter 11 case (R.I. LBR
/// 1007-1(e)).
event Chapter11SchedulesFiled()
/// A creditor whose claim is scheduled as disputed, contingent or
/// unliquidated is added to previously filed chapter 11 schedules (R.I. LBR
/// 1007-1(e)).
event DisputedCreditorAdded()
/// The debtor serves R.I. Local Form 1007-1.1 on the disputed, contingent
/// or unliquidated creditors (R.I. LBR 1007-1(e)).
event DisputedCreditorNoticeServed()
/// The debtor serves an omitted creditor added by amendment with R.I. Local
/// Form 1009-1.1 (R.I. LBR 1009-1(c)).
event AddedCreditorNoticeServed()
/// An order requiring compliance with notice of automatic dismissal, or an
/// order to show cause, is served (R.I. LBR 1017-2(b)).
event ComplianceOrderServed()
/// The date of a proposed Rule 2004 examination (R.I. LBR 2004-1(b)(1)).
event ExaminationScheduled()
/// A motion for a Rule 2004 examination is served (R.I. LBR 2004-1(b)(2)).
event ExaminationMotionServed()
/// The later of the filing of the petition and the date a professional
/// commences rendering services (R.I. LBR 2014-1(c)).
event ProfessionalEngagementBegan()
/// The later of the court's approval of the trustee's appointment and the
/// commencement of the case (R.I. LBR 2015-3(a)).
event InventoryPeriodStarted()
/// A calendar quarter of a chapter 13 business debtor's case ends (R.I. LBR
/// 2015-5(c)).
event QuarterEnded()
/// The Notice of Discharge is issued (R.I. LBR 2016-1(d)).
event DischargeNoticeIssued()
/// An order requesting a fee application from a document preparer is
/// entered (R.I. LBR 2017-1(a)(1)).
event FeeApplicationOrdered()
/// The § 341 meeting is held in a chapter 13 case (R.I. LBR 2017-1(a)(2)).
event MeetingOfCreditorsHeld()
/// A chapter 13 plan is confirmed (R.I. LBR 3007-1(a)).
event Chapter13PlanConfirmed()
/// The deadline for filing proofs of claim in a chapter 13 case passes
/// (R.I. LBR 3007-1(a)).
event ClaimDeadlinePassed()
/// A late proof of claim is filed in a chapter 13 case (R.I. LBR
/// 3007-1(a)).
event LateClaimFiled()
/// An objection to a claim is served (R.I. LBR 3007-1(b)).
event ClaimObjectionServed()
/// A petition for payment of unclaimed funds and its required documents are
/// received and served (R.I. LBR 3011-1(b)(3)).
event UnclaimedFundsPetitionServed()
/// A chapter 13 plan is served on the trustee, creditors and interested
/// parties (R.I. LBR 3015-1(b)).
event PlanServed()
/// The date set for the hearing on confirmation of a chapter 13 plan (R.I.
/// LBR 3015-1(c), 3015-2(b)(1), 3015-3(b)).
event ConfirmationHearingScheduled()
/// A motion to amend a confirmed chapter 13 plan is served (R.I. LBR
/// 3015-2(b)(2)(D)).
event PlanAmendmentMotionServed()
/// An order denying confirmation of a chapter 13 plan is entered (R.I. LBR
/// 3015-3(e)).
event ConfirmationDenied()
/// The court issues a Notice of Intent to Close the Case Without a
/// Discharge for unverified domestic support obligations (R.I. LBR
/// 3015-3(f)(3)).
event CloseWithoutDischargeNoticeIssued()
/// The date set for the hearing on confirmation of a chapter 9 or 11 plan
/// (R.I. LBR 3018-1(b), 3018-2, 3020-1).
event Chapter11ConfirmationHearingScheduled()
/// An order confirming a chapter 11 plan, other than in a subchapter V
/// case, is entered (R.I. LBR 3022-1(a)).
event Chapter11PlanConfirmed()
/// A motion for relief from the automatic stay is served (R.I. LBR
/// 4001-1(d)).
event StayReliefMotionServed()
/// The preliminary hearing on a motion for relief from stay concludes with
/// a final evidentiary hearing scheduled (R.I. LBR 4001-1(i)(1)).
event PreliminaryHearingConcluded()
/// A motion seeking use of cash collateral is served (R.I. LBR 4001-2(c)).
event CashCollateralMotionServed()
/// A chapter 13 borrowing, refinance or loan modification agreement that
/// changes the debtor's income or expenses is executed (R.I. LBR
/// 4001-3(b)).
event BorrowingAgreementExecuted()
/// The clerk sends the lessor notice that the debtor complied with 11
/// U.S.C. § 362(l) (R.I. LBR 4001-4(b)).
event RentDepositNoticeSent()
/// The clerk forwards to an attorney who changed address the notice
/// requesting a designation of cases (R.I. LBR 4002-2).
event AddressChangeNoticeSent()
/// An objection to an exemption is served (R.I. LBR 4003-1(b)).
event ExemptionObjectionServed()
/// A nonconforming document filed with a paid fee is terminated with notice
/// to refile (R.I. LBR 5005-5(a)).
event DocumentTerminated()
/// An order approving a self-represented party's Application and
/// Declaration for the Electronic Drop Box is entered (R.I. LBR
/// 5005-6(a)(2)).
event DropBoxApplicationApproved()
/// The date of a proceeding in which an interpreter's services will be used
/// (R.I. LBR 5007-1(c)).
event ProceedingScheduled()
/// The date the last responsive pleading is required to be filed in an
/// adversary proceeding (R.I. LBR 7008-1(b)).
event LastResponsivePleadingDue()
/// Discovery closes in an adversary proceeding (R.I. LBR 7016(b)).
event DiscoveryClosed()
/// The date the scheduling order is due (R.I. LBR 7026-1(b)).
event SchedulingOrderDue()
/// The parties hold the FRCP 26(f) meeting (R.I. LBR 7026-1(c)).
event PartiesConferred()
/// The clerk dismisses an adversary matter for want of diligent prosecution
/// of the FRCP 26(f) requirements (R.I. LBR 7026-1(d)(1)).
event DismissedForWantOfProsecution()
/// The order determining a timely motion to extend the deadline for a
/// discharge or dischargeability complaint or an exemption objection is
/// entered (R.I. LBR 9006-1).
event ExtensionMotionDetermined()
/// A motion for expedited determination is served (R.I. LBR 9013-2(d)(1)).
event ExpeditedMotionServed()
/// The plaintiff or movant serves the initial draft of a Joint Pretrial
/// Statement (R.I. LBR 9014-1(c)(1)).
event PretrialStatementDraftServed()
/// A Seal Order granting sealing of only portions of a document is entered
/// (R.I. LBR 9018-1(d)(2)).
event PartialSealOrderEntered()
/// A notice of removal is filed under FRBP 9027 (R.I. LBR 9027-1(a)).
event RemovalNoticeFiled()
/// The clerk notifies the parties that trial exhibits should be withdrawn
/// (R.I. LBR 9070-1(c)).
event ExhibitRemovalNoticeIssued()
/// A hearing at which an order is announced in open court is held (R.I. LBR
/// 9072-1(a), 5005-5(b)).
event HearingHeld()
/// An attorney's proposed order or judgment is served for approval as to
/// form (R.I. LBR 9072-1(b)).
event ProposedOrderServed()
/// A motion, application, petition, objection to claim or objection to
/// exemption with the usual response language is served (R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d)(1)).
event PaperServed()
/// An application to compromise is served (R.I. LBR 1005-1(d)(2)(A)).
event CompromiseApplicationServed()
/// A motion or notice of intended sale is served (R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d)(2)(B)).
event SaleNoticeServed()
/// A motion to modify a secured claim is served (R.I. LBR 1005-1(d)(2)(D)).
event SecuredClaimMotionServed()
/// An application or notice to abandon is served (R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d)(2)(E)).
event AbandonmentNoticeServed()
/// An application for compensation is served (R.I. LBR 1005-1(d)(2)(F)).
event CompensationApplicationServed()
/// A motion to vacate an order or to reconsider is served (R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d)(2)(L)).
event ReconsiderationMotionServed()
/// A motion for relief from the co-debtor stay is served (R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d)(2)(M)).
event CodebtorStayMotionServed()
/// A motion to determine under FRBP 3002.1(f) or (g)(4) is served (R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d)(2)(Q), from December 1, 2025).
event MortgageClaimMotionServed()
/// A late document filed without a Motion to File Out of Time, or a timely
/// document defective in form, is stricken (R.I. LBR 1005-1(e)(3)-(4)).
event LateDocumentStricken()
/// An attorney who is not an Electronic Filer conventionally files a first
/// document for a client under the one-time exemption (R.I. LBR
/// 5005-4(c)(2)).
event FirstConventionalFiling()
/// An Electronic Filer files a document whose filing fee is due on filing
/// (R.I. LBR 5005-4(q)).
event FeeBearingDocumentFiled()
/// The date set for the hearing of a matter that is or becomes contested in
/// which an attorney appears pro hac vice without local counsel (R.I. LBR
/// 9010-1(c)).
event ContestedHearingScheduled()

/// R.I. LBR 1007-1(b) and 1002-1(c): the creditor mailing list, the
/// statement of social security number, the debtor's mailing address, the
/// credit counseling certificate or waiver motion and any fee installment
/// or waiver application are filed within 7 days of the bankruptcy filing,
/// or the case is subject to automatic dismissal (R.I. LBR 1007-1(d),
/// 1017-2).
deadline seven-day-documents-period: 7.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1007-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 1002-1(d)(3): a non-individual debtor not represented by
/// counsel at filing obtains counsel within 7 days of the filing date or
/// the case is automatically dismissed, unless relief under R.I. LBR
/// 1017-2(b) was timely requested.
deadline entity-counsel-period: 7.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1002-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 1002-1(d)(4): a petition listing a separate entity as a DBA or
/// FKA is defective, and the debtor files a separate case for that entity
/// within 7 days or the case is subject to automatic dismissal.
deadline separate-entity-petition-period: 7.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1002-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 1006-1(d): an approvable installment schedule pays at least 25%
/// of the fee at filing and continued 25% payments commencing within 30
/// days of the petition date and every 28 days thereafter.
deadline installment-period: 30.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1006-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 1006-1(g): if a fee waiver application is denied and treated as
/// an installment application, the first installment is due within ten days
/// of the order denying the waiver.
deadline waiver-denied-installment-period: 10.days after FeeWaiverDenied() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1006-1(g)"
/// R.I. LBR 1006-1(h): if a chapter 7 case with a waived fee is converted,
/// the debtor pays the full fee for the new chapter, or files an
/// installment application, within 14 days of conversion.
deadline converted-fee-period: 14.days after ConvertedFromWaivedChapter7() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1006-1(h)"
/// R.I. LBR 1007-1(e): the chapter 11 debtor serves R.I. Local Form
/// 1007-1.1 and the proof of claim form on each creditor scheduled as
/// disputed, contingent or unliquidated within 14 days after filing the
/// schedules of liabilities.
deadline disputed-creditor-notice-period: 14.days after Chapter11SchedulesFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1007-1(e)"
/// R.I. LBR 1007-1(e): the notice is served within 14 days of adding such a
/// creditor to previously filed schedules.
deadline added-disputed-creditor-notice-period: 14.days after DisputedCreditorAdded() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1007-1(e)"
/// R.I. LBR 1007-1(e): within 14 days of service of the notice, a
/// certificate evidencing compliance is filed.
deadline disputed-creditor-certificate-period: 14.days after DisputedCreditorNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1007-1(e)"
/// R.I. LBR 1009-1(c)(1)(C): an omitted creditor added by amendment may
/// file complaints under 11 U.S.C. §§ 523 and 727 and objections to
/// exemptions within 60 days of service of the notice, or within the time
/// set for previously scheduled creditors, whichever is later.
deadline added-creditor-objection-period: 60.days after AddedCreditorNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1009-1(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 1017-2(b): the court may dismiss for lack of compliance unless
/// the debtor timely cures or a party requests a hearing within seven days
/// of service of the order requiring compliance.
deadline compliance-hearing-request-period: 7.days after ComplianceOrderServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 1017-2(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 2004-1(b)(1): not less than 14 days' written notice of a
/// proposed Rule 2004 examination is given to the examinee, its counsel and
/// affected parties.
deadline examination-notice-period: 14.days before ExaminationScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2004-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 2004-1(b)(2): an objection or motion for protective order
/// against a Rule 2004 examination is filed within 14 days of service of
/// the motion if served electronically, plus 3 days under FRBP 9006(f) if
/// served by mail.
deadline examination-objection-period: 14.days after ExaminationMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2004-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 2014-1(c): absent extraordinary circumstances nunc pro tunc
/// applications are not considered; an application to employ a professional
/// is timely if filed within 30 days of the later of the petition and the
/// start of services.
deadline employment-application-period: 30.days after ProfessionalEngagementBegan() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2014-1(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 2015-3(a): in chapter 7 and 11 cases other than subchapter V,
/// the FRBP 2015(a)(1) inventory is served on the United States trustee
/// within 30 days after the later of approval of the trustee's appointment
/// and the commencement of the case.
deadline inventory-period: 30.days after InventoryPeriodStarted() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2015-3(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 2015-5(c): a chapter 13 business debtor files and serves on the
/// trustee a statement of the quarter's income and expenses within 30 days
/// of the close of each quarter.
deadline quarterly-statement-period: 30.days after QuarterEnded() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2015-5(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 2015-5(d): a chapter 13 business debtor submits evidence of
/// business insurance to the trustee within 7 days after the commencement
/// of the case.
deadline business-insurance-period: 7.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2015-5(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 2016-1(d)(2): a creditor's final application for the fees of
/// professionals it employs is filed not later than 30 days after the
/// Notice of Discharge.
deadline creditor-final-fee-application-period: 30.days after DischargeNoticeIssued() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2016-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 2017-1(a)(1): a document preparer files a fee application
/// within 21 days of any order requesting it.
deadline preparer-fee-application-period: 21.days after FeeApplicationOrdered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2017-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 2017-1(a)(2): a chapter 13 debtor's attorney whose fee exceeds
/// the Appendix III amounts files a fee application within 60 days after
/// the § 341 meeting is held.
deadline chapter13-fee-application-period: 60.days after MeetingOfCreditorsHeld() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2017-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 2083-1: the debtor and counsel file R.I. Local Form 2083-1.1
/// with the chapter 13 case or within 14 days thereafter.
deadline chapter13-agreement-period: 14.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 2083-1"
/// R.I. LBR 3002-1(d)(3): a claimant secured by the debtor's principal
/// residence may supplement a timely claim with the FRBP 3001(c)(1) and (d)
/// attachments and Local Form 3002-1.1 not later than 120 days after the
/// order for relief or any extension; the December 1, 2025 amendment
/// restates it.
deadline claim-supplement-period: 120.days after OrderForReliefEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3002-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 3003-1: unless the court orders otherwise, proofs of claim in
/// chapter 11 cases are filed on or before 60 days from the date first set
/// for the § 341 meeting; governmental units have the time of 11 U.S.C. §
/// 502(b)(9).
deadline chapter11-claim-period: 60.days after FirstMeetingDate() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3003-1"
/// R.I. LBR 3007-1(a): in chapter 13 cases, objections to claims are filed
/// within 60 days after confirmation of the plan or the claims deadline,
/// whichever is later.
deadline confirmed-claim-objection-period: 60.days after Chapter13PlanConfirmed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3007-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 3007-1(a): within 60 days after the deadline for filing proofs
/// of claim or confirmation, whichever is later.
deadline chapter13-claim-objection-period: 60.days after ClaimDeadlinePassed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3007-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 3007-1(a): an objection to a late filed claim is filed within
/// 60 days after its filing.
deadline late-claim-objection-period: 60.days after LateClaimFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3007-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 3007-1(b): a response to an objection to a claim is filed
/// within 14 days if served electronically, plus 3 days under FRBP 9006 if
/// served by mail.
deadline claim-objection-response-period: 14.days after ClaimObjectionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3007-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 3011-1(b)(3): a 21-day deadline is fixed for objections to a
/// petition for unclaimed funds if served electronically, plus 3 days if
/// served by mail.
deadline unclaimed-funds-objection-period: 21.days after UnclaimedFundsPetitionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3011-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 3015-1(b): a certificate of service of the chapter 13 plan is
/// filed within 14 days after the plan is served.
deadline plan-service-certificate-period: 14.days after PlanServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3015-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 3015-3(b)(1), 3015-1(c)(2) and 3015-2(b)(1): an objection to
/// confirmation of a chapter 13 plan or a pre-confirmation amended plan,
/// including any motion in it, is filed no later than 7 days before the
/// confirmation hearing.
deadline confirmation-objection-period: 7.days before ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3015-3(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 3015-1(c)(3): with a motion to modify a secured claim, the
/// debtor files Supplemental Schedules I and J no later than 7 days prior
/// to the confirmation hearing if allowing the motion changes income or
/// expenses.
deadline supplemental-schedules-period: 7.days before ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3015-1(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 3015-2(b)(2)(D) and 1005-1(d)(2)(C): objections to an amended
/// plan after confirmation are filed no later than 21 days from the date of
/// service of the motion to amend.
deadline confirmed-plan-amendment-objection-period: 21.days after PlanAmendmentMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3015-2(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 3015-3(e): if confirmation is denied, the court may dismiss the
/// case unless within 14 days after the order the debtor files an amended
/// plan, moves to convert, moves for reconsideration, appeals, timely
/// requests relief under R.I. LBR 1017-2(b), or the court orders otherwise.
deadline confirmation-denial-cure-period: 14.days after ConfirmationDenied() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3015-3(e)"
/// R.I. LBR 3015-3(f)(3): the case closes without a discharge unless within
/// 14 days the debtor documents to the trustee that all domestic support
/// obligations are current.
deadline support-obligation-documentation-period: 14.days after CloseWithoutDischargeNoticeIssued() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3015-3(f)"
/// R.I. LBR 3018-1(b): at least 7 days prior to the confirmation hearing,
/// the plan proponent certifies the ballots on R.I. Local Form 3018-1.1.
deadline ballot-certification-period: 7.days before Chapter11ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3018-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 3018-2: a motion to temporarily allow a claim for voting is
/// filed with the ballot at least 14 days prior to confirmation.
deadline temporary-allowance-motion-period: 14.days before Chapter11ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3018-2"
/// R.I. LBR 3020-1(a)-(c): not less than 7 days prior to the confirmation
/// hearing, the plan proponent provides the proposed order of distribution,
/// confirmation worksheet, mailing certification, proposed order and § 1129
/// certification (subchapter V: the documents of (b)), and any proof of
/// deposit is filed.
deadline confirmation-documents-period: 7.days before Chapter11ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3020-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 3020-1(a)(1): the proposed order of distribution, or a notice
/// of its filing, is served on all creditors at least 14 days before the
/// confirmation hearing.
deadline distribution-order-service-period: 14.days before Chapter11ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3020-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 3022-1(a): within six months of the order of confirmation, or
/// sooner on substantial consummation and full administration, the plan
/// proponent files a final report and request for final decree; otherwise a
/// status report (R.I. LBR 3022-1(c)).
deadline final-report-period: 6.months after Chapter11PlanConfirmed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 3022-1(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 4001-1(d): an opposition to a motion for relief from stay is
/// filed within 14 days if served electronically, or 17 days if served
/// under FRBP 9006(f); before an expedited hearing, within 24 hours of it.
deadline stay-relief-opposition-period: 14.days after StayReliefMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4001-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 4001-1(i)(1): the movant delivers a draft joint pretrial
/// statement to the respondent within 7 days of the conclusion of the
/// preliminary hearing.
deadline stay-pretrial-draft-period: 7.days after PreliminaryHearingConcluded() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4001-1(i)"
/// R.I. LBR 4001-2(c): unless the court orders a shorter period, objections
/// to a motion to use cash collateral are filed within 7 days from service.
deadline cash-collateral-objection-period: 7.days after CashCollateralMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4001-2(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 4001-3(b): a chapter 13 debtor files Supplemental Schedules I
/// and J within 14 days of executing a borrowing, refinance or loan
/// modification agreement that changes income or expenses.
deadline borrowing-schedules-period: 14.days after BorrowingAgreementExecuted() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4001-3(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 4001-4(b): the lessor consents to receive the rent deposit or
/// objects within 14 days of the clerk's notice; silence is consent.
deadline lessor-election-period: 14.days after RentDepositNoticeSent() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4001-4(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 4002-2: an attorney who changes address files the designation
/// of cases not to be noticed to the new address within 21 days after the
/// clerk's notice.
deadline address-designation-period: 21.days after AddressChangeNoticeSent() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4002-2"
/// R.I. LBR 4003-1(b): an objection to an exemption carries the R.I. LBR
/// 1005-1(d) notice language with a 14-day response time.
deadline exemption-objection-response-period: 14.days after ExemptionObjectionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 4003-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 5005-5(a): a filer whose fee-paid document is terminated as
/// nonconforming has 14 days to refile it corrected with the fee applied;
/// later, a new fee is required.
deadline corrected-document-period: 14.days after DocumentTerminated() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 5005-5(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 5005-6(a)(2): a self-represented party transmits the original
/// wet-signed Application and Declaration to the clerk within 14 days from
/// the order approving it.
deadline drop-box-signature-period: 14.days after DropBoxApplicationApproved() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 5005-6(a)"
/// R.I. LBR 5007-1(c): a party needing an interpreter files written notice
/// not later than 11 days prior to the proceeding.
deadline interpreter-notice-period: 11.days before ProceedingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 5007-1(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 7008-1(b): the parties consent to a jury trial before the
/// bankruptcy judge by a joint statement no later than 30 days following
/// the date the last responsive pleading is required to be filed.
deadline jury-consent-period: 30.days after LastResponsivePleadingDue() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 7008-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 7016(b): in adversary proceedings a joint pretrial statement is
/// filed within 21 days after the close of discovery unless the court
/// orders otherwise.
deadline adversary-pretrial-statement-period: 21.days after DiscoveryClosed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 7016(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 7026-1(b): the parties meet and confer under FRCP 26(f) within
/// 21 days before the scheduling order is due.
deadline discovery-conference-period: 21.days before SchedulingOrderDue() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 7026-1(b)"
/// R.I. LBR 7026-1(c): within 14 days of the parties' meeting, they file a
/// discovery plan.
deadline discovery-plan-period: 14.days after PartiesConferred() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 7026-1(c)"
/// R.I. LBR 7026-1(d)(1): a plaintiff in default of the FRCP 26(f)
/// requirements may have the dismissed matter reinstated only by motion
/// filed within 14 days of the dismissal.
deadline reinstatement-motion-period: 14.days after DismissedForWantOfProsecution() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 7026-1(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 9006-1: if the court does not determine a timely motion to
/// extend the deadline for a discharge or dischargeability complaint or an
/// exemption objection, the deadline is extended to 7 days after the order
/// determining it, unless the court orders otherwise.
deadline extended-discharge-deadline-period: 7.days after ExtensionMotionDetermined() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 9006-1"
/// R.I. LBR 9013-2(d)(1)(C) and 1005-1(d)(2)(G): written responses to a
/// motion for expedited determination are required within seven days.
deadline expedited-response-period: 7.days after ExpeditedMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "R.I. LBR 9013-2(d)"
/// R.I. LBR 9014-1(c)(1): the opposing party submits comments or revisions
